However, on the flip side, saving endangered species also has profound implications for the health of our planet. Ecosystems provide essential services, like clean water, fertile soil, and the regulation of climate, all of which are critical for human survival. Preserving biodiversity ensures these services remain stable, and losing species could have unforeseen ripple effects that endanger human well-being in the long run. borderWidth:1px;
